  "installation_blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Apply a patch that will install the documentation for this package:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The following command ensures installation of symbolic links are relative:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Ensure the man pages are installed into the correct location:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Prepare Bzip2 for compilation with:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "definition-list",
      "title": "The meaning of the make parameter:",
      "items": [
        {
          "term_content": [
            {
              "type": "parameter",
              "text": "-f Makefile-libbz2_so"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "This will cause Bzip2 to be built using a different"
                },
                {
                  "type": "filename",
                  "text": "Makefile"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "file, in this case the"
                },
                {
                  "type": "filename",
                  "text": "Makefile-libbz2_so"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "file, which creates a dynamic"
                },
                {
                  "type": "filename",
                  "text": "libbz2.so"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "library and links the Bzip2 utilities against it."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Compile and test the package:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Install the programs:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Install the shared library:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The name of the shared library isn't standardized and it varies among distros. The instruction above has installed"
        },
        {
          "type": "filename",
          "text": "libbz2.so.1.0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", but some applications, for example Kbd, expects a different name"
        },
        {
          "type": "filename",
          "text": "libbz2.so.1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "that some other distros are using. Create a compatibility symlink for them:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "kind": "note",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The symlink approach is only valid here because the library name difference is a result of different aesthetic views of the distro maintainers, not real ABI incompatibilities. In general a library name difference most likely indicates an ABI incompatibility and it would be very likely invalid to"
            },
            {
              "type": "quote",
              "text": "hide"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "the difference via a symlink. Read"
            },
            {
              "type": "xref",
              "target": "pkgmgmt-upgrade-issues",
              "label": "Upgrade Issues"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "for details about library names."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Install the shared"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "bzip2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "binary into the"
        },
        {
          "type": "filename",
          "text": "/usr/bin"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "directory, and replace two copies of"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "bzip2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "with symlinks:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 8
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Remove a useless static library:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 9
    }
